                <mxCell id="e0xKdjC2LP675MrJmHpH-18" value="AV1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="500" y="190" width="50" height="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e0xKdjC2LP675MrJmHpH-19" value="AV1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="500" y="270" width="50" height="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e0xKdjC2LP675MrJmHpH-20" value="&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DDI layer:&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;Connect to libva,&amp;nbsp; and implement all the DDI functions.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Device Manager&lt;/b&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63);&quot;&gt;Open media device for decoding or encoding, and m&lt;/span&gt;anage all the VA buffers/surfaces used by all the codecs. It creates codecs (&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63);&quot;&gt;V4L2 Stateful decoder or encoder&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;in CreateContext(), and then calls into the codec object to create V4L2 buffers which will be bound with different VA surfaces or VA buffers. It resides between codec and DDI layer to pass data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;The following objects are maintained in device manager:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Video codecs&lt;/b&gt;: one device could have multiple codec instances opened.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Surface&lt;/b&gt;: Used as decode output or encode input. One surface can be used by different codecs.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Buffers&lt;/b&gt;: All the codec input/output data should be stored in buffers.&amp;nbsp; Buffer memory can be in system DMA heap or normal system memory.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;V4L2 Stateful Decoder&lt;/b&gt;: Maintains V4L2 M2M stateful decoder specific methods and data. It also creates packer and parser to repack headers for different video formats, like SPS, PPS and slice header.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63); scrollbar-color: rgb(226, 226, 226) rgb(251, 251, 251);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63); scrollbar-color: rgb(226, 226, 226) rgb(251, 251, 251); background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63); scrollbar-color: rgb(226, 226, 226) rgb(251, 251, 251);&quot;&gt;V4L2 Stateful Encoder&lt;/b&gt;: Maintains V4L2 M2M stateful encoder specific methods and data. It also creates extractor to fetch useful parameters for encoder configuration.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Packer&lt;/b&gt;: video format specific logics for header packing, including emulation prevention bytes adding. Different video formats should have different implementation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Parser&lt;/b&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63);&quot;&gt;video format specific logics for&amp;nbsp;header parsing, including emulation prevention bytes removing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Different video formats should have different implementation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Extractor&lt;/b&gt;: Extract required encode parameters from&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;VAEncSequenceParameterBufferXXX, VAEncPictureParameterBufferXXX and&amp;nbsp;VAEncSliceParameterBufferXXX, like coded buffer ID, GOP size, B frames, frame QP, etc. Used by Encoder only.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Log System&lt;/b&gt;: debug log control&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="120" y="540" width="560" height="490" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="IlsXHJPclxPX1hFeky2A-1" value="Extractor" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=bottom;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="370" y="340" width="190" height="70" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
